# Controlled Bevy example

This package is a small context-menu application used by the automation smoke test.

Without features it is a normal native Bevy application. With `--features automation`, the Debug
Host starts a Controlled Session that disables native input and accepts only protocol-v2 Virtual
Input commands. The `bevy_controller` example drives pointer movement, buttons, scroll-capable
pointer state, keyboard press and release, and text entry into a focused `EditableText`. It observes
the reflected application state after each path.
